From 83f1ef157a19a1c69218b579386354d74a9f7110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:47:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 079/108] gpu: vulkan: shader translation on the creation
 threads; ui: FSR 1.0 / CAS without the FidelityFX SDK

Pipeline creation was asynchronous (vulkan_pipeline_compile_never_blocks) but
the SPIR-V translation of a new shader still ran on the GPU thread, 14-24 ms
each on the Thor: 25 of them in one 10-second window at a battle entry. With
vulkan_async_shader_translation (default on) the GPU thread only runs the
ucode analysis, which is all the pipeline description needs, and queues the
pipeline; the creation thread translates (one translator shared under a
mutex) and computes the pipeline layout, which depends on the bindings known
after translation (the command processor's layout getters already lock). The
translation's translated/valid flags are atomics with "translated" stored
last; the command processor skips a draw whose shader was untranslated when
its textures were requested and whose pipeline got published meanwhile. A
creation-thread failure no longer leaves a pending entry pending forever.

The presenter's in-tree AMD FSR 1.0 (EASU + RCAS) and CAS paint effects were
gated behind the optional FidelityFX SDK together with FSR2/3; they are now
under an always-on REX_HAS_FIDELITYFX_SPATIAL, so present_effect = bilinear |
cas | fsr and the CAS/FSR sharpness cvars work without the SDK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

